 "summary": {
  "headline": "Anand Rathi Wealth Q1 FY27: underlying PAT up 24% YoY to INR116 crore; AUM up 21% to INR1,06,300 crore.",
  "overview": "Management reported its 19th consecutive quarter of profit growth, with underlying (ex fair value gains, ESOP and tax effects) consolidated revenue of INR336 crore (+18% YoY) and PAT of INR116 crore (+24% YoY), a 34.4% margin. Reported revenue including fair value gains was INR430 crore and PAT INR163 crore, with INR110 crore of other income, of which INR96 crore was mark-to-market gain on the Anand Rathi Global Finance holding. Q1 delivered 24% of FY27 revenue guidance (INR1,415 crore) and 25% of PAT guidance (INR460 crore). AUM reached INR1,06,300 crore with net flows of INR2,743 crore, and client AUM attrition was 0.09%. Management also disclosed Board approval to apply for an AMC licence and progress on UK and GIFT City subsidiaries.",
  "financial_highlights": [
   {
